From: Chen Minqiang <ptpt52@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: motorcomm: select PHY_PACKAGE for phy package support

The YT8824 quad-port 2.5G PHY support added in the motorcomm driver
uses phy_package helpers (devm_of_phy_package_join, phy_package_probe_once,
phy_package_get_priv, phy_package_get_node, __phy_package_read,
__phy_package_write) but the Kconfig entry for MOTORCOMM_PHY is missing
'select PHY_PACKAGE', causing link errors when PHY_PACKAGE is not
otherwise enabled.

Add the missing 'select PHY_PACKAGE' to fix the build.

Fixes: 799-36 ("net: phy: Add driver for Motorcomm Quad 2.5GbE phy")
Signed-off-by: Chen Minqiang <ptpt52@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/phy/Kconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/drivers/net/phy/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/Kconfig
@@ -423,6 +423,7 @@ config MICROSEMI_PHY
 
 config MOTORCOMM_PHY
 	tristate "Motorcomm PHYs"
+	select PHY_PACKAGE
 	help
 	  Enables support for Motorcomm network PHYs.
 	  Currently supports YT85xx Gigabit Ethernet PHYs.
